### Telecom order API – IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client
### Email triggers: slow, down, risky, provfail, manual
@api = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### Place an order (CompletableFuture workflow) -> 201 PROVISIONING
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerName":"Anita Rao","email":"anita@example.com","planCode":"UNL-599","circle":"KA"}

### Long-poll until final (DeferredResult): 200 when ACTIVE/FAILED/REJECTED, 202 when the wait expires
GET {{api}}/orders/REPLACE_WITH_ID/await?timeoutSeconds=20

### Order without automatic callback (complete it with the webhook below)
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerName":"Manual","email":"manual@example.com","planCode":"DATA-299","circle":"TN"}

### Provisioning webhook (applied=false for duplicates / late callbacks)
POST {{api}}/provisioning/callbacks
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId":"REPLACE_WITH_ID","success":true,"iccid":"8991000000000000001","message":"activated"}

### Failure modes
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerName":"Slow","email":"slow@example.com","planCode":"UNL-599","circle":"KA"}

### Cached plan lookup (second call is instant)
GET {{api}}/plans/FAM-999

### Parallel bulk portability check
POST {{api}}/portability/bulk-check
Content-Type: application/json

["9876543210","9876543211","9000000001","9001000001"]

### Orders by status
GET {{api}}/orders?status=ACTIVE&size=10
